From c527d187e7c2299621acdb1928ede8061f79ccd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:56:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] Fix: the Momentum Ladder discarded every paper setup it
 generated

The Ladder's paper watchlist has been empty since the lifecycle was introduced.
old_nse_hull_paper_state.json is written on schedule -- updated_at moves every
day -- but watchlist, positions and events have never contained a single entry.

Cause
-----
paper_lifecycle.update built one lookup:

    candidate_map = {str(row["symbol"]): row for row in (market_rows or candidates)}

and used it for two incompatible purposes: advancing held positions, which needs
completed OHLC for every observed symbol, and admitting new watchlist entries,
which needs trade_levels. The shadow engine always passes market_rows -- every
enriched row, so a held symbol that drops out of today's candidates still gets
its stop checked, which is correct -- but those rows carry no trade_levels,
because run_shadow attaches them only to the qualified candidates frame. So the
"market_rows or candidates" expression silently resolved to the rows without
levels, eligible_for_paper was never seen, and nothing was ever admitted.

Measured on 2026-08-20: 282 qualified candidates, 117 with a valid entry, stop
and risk under 8%. Admitted: zero.

Fix
---
 old_nse_hull/multi_horizon/paper_lifecycle.py |  31 ++-
 scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py               | 217 ++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_ladder_paper_admission.py          | 186 +++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 432 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py
 create mode 100755 tests/test_ladder_paper_admission.py

